Package: multihostSIR
Type: Package
Title: multihostSIR – an R package for simulating multi-host pathogen dynamics in ecological communities
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mayank", "Gangwar", email = "mayankgangwar10@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Andrew", "Kramer", email = "amkramer@usf.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Builds and simulates Susceptible-Infected-Recovered (SIR) models for
    an arbitrary number of interacting host species. Species-specific mortality,
    recovery, carrying capacity and virulence may be derived from body mass using
    quarter-power allometric scaling (Kleiber, 1932, <doi:10.1093/jn/6.4.315>;
    Damuth, 1981, <doi:10.1038/290699a0>), and between-species transmission is
    described by an asymmetric matrix built from within-species transmission rates
    and trophic interaction coefficients. Community-level basic reproduction
    numbers are obtained as the dominant eigenvalue of the next-generation matrix
    (Diekmann, Heesterbeek and Metz, 1990, <doi:10.1007/BF00178324>). Utilities are
    provided for randomised replicate communities, run-time scaling studies,
    summary tables and publication-quality figures.
